<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO LOOKING AT HUNGARY'S MHB BANK.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO LOOKING AT HUNGARY'S MHB BANK.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch bank ABN AMRO NV said on Thursday it was looking at Hungary's state-owned Magyar Hitel Bank (MHB), which is being privatised.</p>
<p>&quot;We have been invited by the Hungarians to take a look at it. I can't say whether we will be interested,&quot; ABN AMRO's chief spokesman Jules Prast told Reuters.</p>
<p>Hungary has invited three unnamed banks to bid for MHB. Media reports suggest the other possible buyers include Austria's two largest banks, Bank Austria and Creditanstalt , and U.S. giant Citibank .</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
